                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
                    "body": "> `grep_live` is a very special picker with a very special `source.match`.\r\n\r\nBasically, I want to write a custom matcher specifically for the grep picker that will parse input like `name | glob, glob, glob`. Now, it seems more sensible to write the picker from scratch.\r\n\r\nI thought it could be done like with the `show` field:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal minipick_grep_live_match = function(stritems, inds, query_tbl, opts)\r\n  -- Modify `query_tbl`\r\n  return MiniPick.default_match(stritems, inds, query_tbl, opts)\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\n> `<C-o>` as a special picker mapping\r\n\r\nI wanted to disable or override it:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  MiniPick.builtin.grep_live({}, {\r\n    mappings = {\r\n      aa_override = {\r\n        char = \"<C-o>\",\r\n        func = function()\r\n          -- Doesn't work\r\n          vim.print(\"+\")\r\n        end,\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n  })\r\n```\r\n\r\nI needed to think a bit harder before asking. Maybe I can’t quite get used to multiple models of defining mappings.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">grep_live</code> is a very special picker with a very special <code class=\"notranslate\">source.match</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Basically, I want to write a custom matcher specifically for the grep picker that will parse input like <code class=\"notranslate\">name | glob, glob, glob</code>. Now, it seems more sensible to write the picker from scratch.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I thought it could be done like with the <code class=\"notranslate\">show</code> field:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local minipick_grep_live_match = function(stritems, inds, query_tbl, opts)\n  -- Modify `query_tbl`\n  return MiniPick.default_match(stritems, inds, query_tbl, opts)\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">minipick_grep_live_match</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">stritems</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">inds</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">query_tbl</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Modify `query_tbl`</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">default_match</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">stritems</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">inds</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">query_tbl</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-o&gt;</code> as a special picker mapping</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I wanted to disable or override it:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"  MiniPick.builtin.grep_live({}, {\n    mappings = {\n      aa_override = {\n        char = &quot;&lt;C-o&gt;&quot;,\n        func = function()\n          -- Doesn't work\n          vim.print(&quot;+&quot;)\n        end,\n      },\n    },\n  })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">  <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">builtin</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">grep_live</span>({}, {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">mappings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n      <span class=\"pl-smi\">aa_override</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n        <span class=\"pl-smi\">char</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;C-o&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n        <span class=\"pl-en\">func</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n          <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Doesn't work</span>\n          <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">print</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>+<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n      },\n    },\n  })</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I needed to think a bit harder before asking. Maybe I can’t quite get used to multiple models of defining mappings.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "grep_live is a very special picker with a very special source.match.\n\nBasically, I want to write a custom matcher specifically for the grep picker that will parse input like name | glob, glob, glob. Now, it seems more sensible to write the picker from scratch.\nI thought it could be done like with the show field:\nlocal minipick_grep_live_match = function(stritems, inds, query_tbl, opts)\n  -- Modify `query_tbl`\n  return MiniPick.default_match(stritems, inds, query_tbl, opts)\nend\n\n<C-o> as a special picker mapping\n\nI wanted to disable or override it:\n  MiniPick.builtin.grep_live({}, {\n    mappings = {\n      aa_override = {\n        char = \"<C-o>\",\n        func = function()\n          -- Doesn't work\n          vim.print(\"+\")\n        end,\n      },\n    },\n  })\nI needed to think a bit harder before asking. Maybe I can’t quite get used to multiple models of defining mappings.",
