                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "I am afraid, `grep_live` is indeed a very special picker which is also quite fragile. I would like to avoid having to update and/or rewrite it to account for possible \"hacking\". It is indeed better to write custom picker to fully own the \"live\" part of the implementation.\r\n\r\n> I guess it can be done like this:\r\n\r\nProbably, not 100% of the time. The `<C-o>` key might be associated either with `add_glob` or `aa_override`. There is no order guarantee of how actions are matched to their keys.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I am afraid, <code class=\"notranslate\">grep_live</code> is indeed a very special picker which is also quite fragile. I would like to avoid having to update and/or rewrite it to account for possible \"hacking\". It is indeed better to write custom picker to fully own the \"live\" part of the implementation.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I guess it can be done like this:</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Probably, not 100% of the time. The <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-o&gt;</code> key might be associated either with <code class=\"notranslate\">add_glob</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">aa_override</code>. There is no order guarantee of how actions are matched to their keys.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "I am afraid, grep_live is indeed a very special picker which is also quite fragile. I would like to avoid having to update and/or rewrite it to account for possible \"hacking\". It is indeed better to write custom picker to fully own the \"live\" part of the implementation.\n\nI guess it can be done like this:\n\nProbably, not 100% of the time. The <C-o> key might be associated either with add_glob or aa_override. There is no order guarantee of how actions are matched to their keys.",
